{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":27.600000381469727,"text":"small jars of roots, bark, leaves, and dried flowers. Before chemical colors, every dye came from a plant. Yellow from saffron or onion skins, red from madder root, blue from indigo, brown from walnut husk. Color does not hold on its own. It needs something to fix it to the wool. That is why dyeing was a trade and not a trick. Get it wrong, and the color goes in the first wash.","words":[{"word":"small","start":0,"end":0.800000011920929},{"word":"jars","start":0.800000011920929,"end":1.100000023841858},{"word":"of","start":1.100000023841858,"end":1.9600000381469727},{"word":"roots","start":1.9600000381469727,"end":1.9600000381469727},{"word":"bark","start":2.5999999046325684,"end":2.5999999046325684},{"word":"leaves","start":3.319999933242798,"end":3.319999933242798},{"word":"and","start":3.440000057220459,"end":3.9600000381469727},{"word":"dried","start":3.9600000381469727,"end":3.9600000381469727},{"word":"flowers","start":3.9600000381469727,"end":4.460000038146973},{"word":"Before","start":5.21999979019165,"end":5.440000057220459},{"word":"chemical","start":5.440000057220459,"end":5.860000133514404},{"word":"colors","start":5.860000133514404,"end":6.239999771118164},{"word":"every","start":6.71999979019165,"end":7.199999809265137},{"word":"dye","start":7.199999809265137,"end":7.460000038146973},{"word":"came","start":7.460000038146973,"end":7.820000171661377},{"word":"from","start":7.820000171661377,"end":7.980000019073486},{"word":"a","start":7.980000019073486,"end":8.5},{"word":"plant","start":8.5,"end":8.5},{"word":"Yellow","start":9.359999656677246,"end":9.359999656677246},{"word":"from","start":9.359999656677246,"end":9.699999809265137},{"word":"saffron","start":9.699999809265137,"end":10.220000267028809},{"word":"or","start":10.220000267028809,"end":10.520000457763672},{"word":"onion","start":10.520000457763672,"end":10.859999656677246},{"word":"skins","start":10.859999656677246